choice BT_THREAD_SCHEDULER_LOCK
  prompt "Enable Bluetooth Thread Scheduler Lock"
  default BT_THREAD_SCHEDULER_LOCK_VIA_HIGHEST_PRIO
  help
    Enable the Bluetooth thread scheduler lock to protect critical sections in the Bluetooth stack.
    This ensures thread-safe operations when accessing shared resources in the Bluetooth
    implementation.

  config BT_THREAD_SCHEDULER_LOCK_VIA_HIGHEST_PRIO
    bool "Set current thread with highest priority for Bluetooth Thread Scheduler Lock"
    help
      Set current thread with highest priority for Bluetooth Thread Scheduler Lock. This provides
      a simple and efficient mechanism for synchronizing access to critical sections in the
      Bluetooth stack.

  config BT_THREAD_SCHEDULER_LOCK_VIA_SCHEDULER
    bool "Use Scheduler for Bluetooth Thread Scheduler Lock"
    help
      Use the scheduler's built-in locking mechanism to implement the Bluetooth thread scheduler
      lock. This may provide better performance in certain scenarios but may not be supported on all
      platforms. But, the potential issue is the synchronize components cannot be used in Edgefast
      open Bluetooth callback, including `xQueuePeek()`, `xQueueSemaphoreTake()`, `xQueueReceive()`,
      `xQueueGenericSend()`, `xEventGroupWaitBits()`, `xEventGroupSync()`, etc.

  config BT_THREAD_SCHEDULER_LOCK_NONE
    bool "Do not use Bluetooth Thread Scheduler Lock"
    help
      Do not use any locking mechanism for the Bluetooth thread scheduler. This may lead to
      potential race conditions and is not recommended for production use.

endchoice # BT_THREAD_SCHEDULER_LOCK

config THREAD_NAME
  bool "Enable custom thread naming"
  default y
  help
    Enable support for custom thread names in the Bluetooth thread implementation.

